// DiscoveryList Discovery lists for browsing. `most-played`, `recently-played`, `starred`, `never-played`, `rediscover`, and `in-progress` reflect the calling user's own listening state.
// `never-played` is what the caller has never counted a play of, and `rediscover` is what they starred or rated at least 80 and have not played in six months (never counts as six months, so something starred and never reached belongs there). "Played" on both is the same threshold `playCount` counts, so an item abandoned early enough to have never crossed it is still sealed.
// Both come back A to Z, since neither is ordered by anything a listener would recognize: there is no play stamp to sort a never-played item by, and sorting the other by how stale it is would put the most forgotten thing first every time the shelf is drawn. The others keep the orders their names describe.
// `in-progress` is what the caller is part way through: a saved position on something not finished, most recently progressed first. An episode or an audiobook is on it from its first saved position, whether or not a play has counted. A track is on it only once a play of it has counted, the membership `recently-played` has: a position is saved for a track skipped a few seconds in as for any other, and that is not something to carry on with.
type DiscoveryList string

